                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "the game, for as interesting of a concept as it sounds like, is unplayable.\n\nsurviving even just 2 minutes in the death can that is your ship is impossible, the goal of the game is to make it through 20+ minutes of charging before you can leave the combat area and do... something else, i don't know, i haven't played that far in yet.\n\nthe difficulty curve feels more like a difficulty wall, i'm pretty confident that the game cannot be beat with a curve this sharp.\n\nthe upgrade screens are rather simple to use, i learned them all very quickly, but the computer in which you have to enter commands, urgh! please, add a command which will make it easier figuring out what does what, i can't even figure out whether it's even meant to be used right now.\n\nand the personal computer!... i'm honestly not sure what you're supposed to do at it, i've gone inside the different types of messages, not sure whether the message de-coder is doing anything, but i feel like the pc itself is useless.\n\ni understand that the game is still just fresh after development and in need of tweaking... but i honestly did not expect the difficulty curve to be an issue, i feel as it is the most basic thing you could have done, it's as if you didn't even play-test the game before releasing it.\n\ni don't see many bugs inside of it, but in its' current state, it's unplayable, the difficulty curve needs to be tweaked so the first 5 minutes can actually be survived, and the gun you're given... it isn't a problem, but with how many points i had to spend to even get through a minute and a half of the game, i think you need to consider the gun's upgrades as well as the ship's upgrades.\n\nthat is all i have to say, i'll keep looking as the development of the game unfolds, but currently it's anything but enjoyable, the experience for me was filled with irritation and anger, please fix the difficulty curve.",
